{"id": "EUVD-2026-101278", "enisaUuid": "61af5082-d8b1-3dfa-836d-4a6b1241ae82", "description": "The thumbnail Python package through 1.5 contains an OS command injection vulnerability in generate_thumbnail() that allows attackers to execute commands by supplying shell metacharacters in file paths. Attackers who control a file name passed to generate_thumbnail, such as an uploaded file, can inject commands into os.system() calls running ffmpeg, convert or unoconv with the Python process privileges.", "datePublished": "2026-10-14T14:17:17", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-14T20:38:22", "baseScore": 9.3, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:L/AT:N/PR:N/UI:N/VC:H/VI:H/VA:H/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N", "references": ["https://github.com/anshulkharb/thumbnail/pull/9", "https://github.com/anshulkharb/thumbnail/blob/23b2e30509c936872a3bafac65b4aa48777e794c/thumbnail/thumbnail.py#L100-L114", "https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/thumbnail-through-1.5-os-command-injection-via-generate-thumbnail-file-paths"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-110650", "GHSA-542h-xc5c-6hxm"], "assigner": "VulnCheck", "epss": 2.99, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "0e111220-d59b-398c-a73a-3255afe34dce", "product": {"name": "thumbnail", "vendor": {"name": "anshulkharb"}}, "product_version": "0 \u22641.5"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "8f044687-43a9-3d88-9725-92189d5056ce", "vendor": {"name": "anshulkharb"}}], "isExploited": false}